## Detailed Component Specifications

### 1. Frontend Components (`frontend/`)
- **`index.html`**: Structured semantic wrapper containing navigation bar, system stats grid, main visualization panel, file drop area, model parameters tuning panel, real-time alert feed table, and explainability modal.
- **`styles.css`**: Complete design system defining CSS variables, dark glassmorphism styling, alert severity visual indicators, pulse animations, custom scrollbars, and mobile responsiveness.
- **`app.js`**: Core UI state controller managing API communication, dynamic Chart.js canvas updating, dataset ingestion parsing, stream timer loop, sensitivity slider debouncing, and explainability modal popups.

### 2. Backend Components (`backend/`)
- **`main.py`**: FastAPI entry point, CORS middleware, API router inclusion, static file mounting.
- **`schemas.py`**: Pydantic schemas validating prediction payloads, stream requests, alert objects, dataset uploads, model configs, and system health status.
- **`routes.py`**: Handles API endpoints (`/api/predict`, `/api/stream/next`, `/api/datasets/upload`, `/api/datasets/sample`, `/api/models`, `/api/alerts`, `/api/health`).

### 3. ML Engine Components (`ml_module/`)
- **`detector.py`**: Multi-algorithm wrapper (`IsolationForest`, `LocalOutlierFactor`, `OneClassSVM`, `Z-Score`). Standardizes predictions into uniform output format.
- **`preprocessor.py`**: Handles numerical feature extraction, missing value imputation, scaling, and rolling temporal statistics.
- **`explainer.py`**: Evaluates individual metric Z-scores and produces feature attribution percentage breakdowns explaining why a point was flagged.
- **`generator.py`**: Generates multi-metric telemetry frames with synthetic anomalies (Point Spikes, Contextual Drift, Collective Errors).